# 🔍 BitCurator 5 Digital Forensics & Archival Workstation (Kasm-Enhanced)

An advanced digital forensics and data curation environment built on top of `squirrelworksllc/ubuntu-noble-core`. This image seamlessly pairs the full BitCurator 5 SaltStack software catalog with the lightweight, high-performance runtime performance of modern Kasm Workspaces.

## ✔️ Included Tool Ecosystem

*   **Forensic Imaging & Triage:** Guymager, Nwipe, Disktype
*   **Filesystem Forensics:** The Sleuth Kit (TSK), Fiwalk, BitCurator Reports
*   **Data Identification & NLP:** Bulk Extractor, BitCurator NLP, Brunnhilde, RegEx tools
*   **Malware & File Analysis:** ClamAV, Hashdeep, Fido, Siegfried
*   **Code & Script Analysis:** Visual Studio Code (pre-configured), Python3 toolkit

## 🎯 Purpose

This workstation provides a standardized, immutable, and completely isolated sandbox environment designed specifically for digital archivists, institutional curators, and forensic researchers. It is tailored for:

*   Executing interactive disk imaging and legacy data curation safely inside container boundaries.
*   Conducting metadata extraction, PII identification, and digital preservation workflows.
*   Serving as a reproducible remote forensics and archival workstation within the Kasm 1.18 platform architecture.
